                                "example_id": "e54afc75-bd13-4b97-a310-720d903776dc",
                                "sense_id": "a3ac6577-abcf-3b10-a356-d1557e5402ea",
                                "text": "The cothons at Carthage, during the Punic wars, are said to have held over two hundred ships. The small size of the Motya cothon may be accounted for by […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8b0d205-5274-462d-970f-0e0f8ec8251f",
                                "sense_id": "a3ac6577-abcf-3b10-a356-d1557e5402ea",
                                "text": "Cothons - artificial inner harbours, or perhaps rather docks and repair basins - are another architectural feature ascribed to Phoenician and Punic towns […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a5cc79e-8fb7-422b-baf6-db6f1fc33a09",
                                "sense_id": "a3ac6577-abcf-3b10-a356-d1557e5402ea",
                                "text": "It resembles the Phoenician cothons'."
